From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 05 Nov 2026 22:57:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: leave the NPU tx free ring to the NPU at queue init

With NPU offload, the NPU owns the tx free ring of the chip: it puts
its own buffers into that ring and reads each event. Rx queue init
also fills this ring with host buffers and moves its CPU index. The
chip then prefetches descriptors that point at host buffers, and
writes its first events there. No reader takes these events, so
tokens of the first frames stay allocated.

Skip the fill of this ring, as rx queue reset does.

Fixes: 2bc891cc94e0 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: Do not schedule RRO and TxFree queues during reset for NPU")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 dma.c |    6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -1127,8 +1127,12 @@ static void
 mt76_dma_rx_queue_init(struct mt76_dev *dev, enum mt76_rxq_id qid,
 		       int (*poll)(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget))
 {
+	struct mt76_queue *q = &dev->q_rx[qid];
+
 	netif_napi_add(dev->napi_dev, &dev->napi[qid], poll);
-	mt76_dma_rx_fill_buf(dev, &dev->q_rx[qid], false);
+	/* The NPU puts its own buffers into its tx free ring */
+	if (!mt76_queue_is_npu_txfree(q))
+		mt76_dma_rx_fill_buf(dev, q, false);
 	napi_enable(&dev->napi[qid]);
 }
 
